{"type":"system","subtype":"background_tasks_changed","tasks":[{"task_id":"bhi1lfit2","task_type":"local_bash","description":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4\nSRC=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/gamblers_second_order_person_lapse.py\necho signed_sensitivity_person_lapse > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `gamblers_second_order_person_lapse` (people judge a sequence random to the extent their own second-order, gambler's-fallacy model of a fair coin explains it better than the regular generators they suspect — a switch-biased coin, a biased coin, a repeating short motif with slips — weighed per flip by a fitted power of length, with person-specific side habits and person-specific random lapses). The single change is that people do not all read regularity as a sign of non-randomness: each person's sensitivity to the \"regular generator versus chance\" evidence is drawn from a population that can straddle zero instead of being forced positive, so a minority of participants systematically treat patterned, streaky or periodic sequences as the more random-looking ones (or invert the judgment) and agree with the majority below chance even on clear-cut pairs — addressing the FDR-surviving critique that participants differ in their rate of agreeing with the majority more than the incumbent's lapses and positive sensitivities produce.\nEOF\npython3 - << EOF\nsrc=open(\"$SRC\").read()\nold='''    mu_log_beta = pm.Normal(\"mu_log_beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_log_beta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_log_beta\", sigma=0.5)\n    z_beta = pm.Normal(\"z_beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    beta = pt.exp(mu_log_beta + sigma_log_beta * z_beta)'''\nnew='''    # Single change: signed person-specific sensitivity (normal population that\n    # may straddle zero), so some people read regularity as randomness.\n    mu_beta = pm.Normal(\"mu_beta\", mu=1.0, sigma=1.0)\n    sigma_beta = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_beta\", sigma=1.0)\n    z_beta = pm.Normal(\"z_beta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    beta = mu_beta + sigma_beta * z_beta'''\nassert old in src\nsrc=src.replace(old,new)\nhead='''\"\"\"Signed person-specific sensitivity to regularity evidence, refining gamblers_second_order_person_lapse.\n\nRefinement of `gamblers_second_order_person_lapse`. Single change: each person's\nsensitivity beta_i to the (second-order, gambler's-fallacy chance coin versus\nregular generators) evidence is drawn from a normal population that can straddle\nzero, instead of a log-normal (positive-only) one, so a minority of participants\ncan treat regular sequences as the more random ones and agree with the majority\nbelow chance even on clear-cut pairs. Addresses the FDR-surviving critique that\nparticipants' agreement with the majority varies more than the incumbent produces.\n\nDescription of the incumbent:\n'''\nsrc=head+src[3:]\nopen(\"$D/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},{"task_id":"byxsvvhqc","task_type":"local_bash","description":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4; sed -i '3s/Refinement of \\. /Refinement of `gamblers_second_order_person_lapse`. /' $D/candidate.py; sed -n 3p $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratc